### What pa3ds calls X and Y's pictures that the game never names. Said whole as the cursor comes
### onto each (`games.xy.intro`).

# The opening's choice of boy or girl, each in a mirror, and then the three looks of the one
# chosen, each a portrait in a frame. These are models with no layout and no name to key on
# (spike 216), so each is keyed by what the intro's work says is under the cursor: the mirror's
# `model-boy` or `model-girl`, and the portrait's `model-<boy or girl>_<left, middle or right>`.
#
# Read off the replays' pictures, enlarged (x_character-desc.ctm and x_character-desc2.ctm,
# 2026-10-15); the shoes from the camera's pan up the chosen one's mirror after the name, since
# the mirrors' own screen cuts both off at the shins. The three looks of each differ only in skin,
# hair and eyes: every boy wears the red cap and blue jacket the boy in the mirror does, and every
# girl the pink hat and black blouse.
model-boy = Boy, fair skin, short black hair, blue-grey eyes, red cap with dark sunglasses on top, royal-blue zip-up track jacket with a high collar and white stripes, black bag strap across the chest, dark-blue jeans, grey lace-up boots
model-girl = Girl, fair skin, long wavy honey-blonde hair, blue eyes, rose-pink hat with white-framed sunglasses on top, black sleeveless blouse with a bow at the collar, red high-waisted pleated skirt, pink quilted handbag, black thigh-high stockings, grey high-top lace-up shoes with a buckled ankle strap
model-boy_left = Pale skin, platinum-blond hair in spiky strands, bright blue eyes, small closed smile
model-boy_middle = Fair skin, black hair in a short bob, blue-grey eyes, open cheerful smile
model-boy_right = Brown skin, dark grey-black hair in a short bob, amber-brown eyes, calm closed smile
model-girl_left = Pale skin, long platinum-blonde hair, bright blue eyes, open smile with red lips
model-girl_middle = Fair skin, long wavy honey-blonde hair, blue-grey eyes, gentle closed smile
model-girl_right = Brown skin, long wavy dark grey-black hair, amber-brown eyes, gentle closed smile

# The Pokémon-Amie page's menu, opened by tapping its Pokémon. X draws its three buttons as
# pictures of their words, `kwg_button01` PLAY in the middle, `02` DECORATE on the left and `03`
# SWITCH on the right, and has no line of text for them. These are Omega Ruby's own words for the
# same buttons, its text file 123 lines 77 to 79, in each language it carries (spike 228,
# x_super_train3).
texture-kwg_button01 = PLAY
texture-kwg_button02 = DECORATE
texture-kwg_button03 = SWITCH

# Words the title screen draws as pictures, as a sighted player reads them, said in its
# description (`{ PICTURE("push_start") }`): its blinking prompt, `push_start`, and the studio's
# credit at the end of the bottom screen's reel, which X and Y draw into the reel itself, with no
# texture, and Omega Ruby as `presented_by` and `gf_logo`, the names it is said by here
# (x_intro_and_title_screen).
texture-push_start = Press Start
texture-presented_by = Presented by
texture-gf_logo = Game Freak
